  "preamble": "Retraction of the velar nasal [ŋ] to the uvular nasal [ɴ] by place assimilation to a following uvular consonant. In Kazakh, /ŋ/ (ң) is realized as [ɴ] before the uvulars /q/ and /ʁ/ (the latter then surfacing as a stop [ɢ] after the nasal), as in даңқ /dɑŋq/ [d̥ɑ̝ɴqʰ] 'glory'. In Khalkha Mongolian, /ŋ/ is uvular [ɴ] before /ɢ/ and before /x/, which is itself uvular [χ] in back-vowel words, as in монгол /mɔŋ.ɢɔɮ/ [ˈmɔ̙ɴ.ɢɞ̙̆ɮ]. Dutch speakers who pronounce /x, ɣ/ as uvular likewise have [ɴ] for /ŋ/ before them.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Place Assimilation, Retraction, Uvularization",
